# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — copy to .env and fill in real values before running the stack.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        (Linux / macOS / Git Bash)
#   copy .env.example .env      (Windows CMD)
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env (Windows PowerShell)
#
# .env is gitignored — never commit it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Downloads folder (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The host path to your OS Downloads folder. Docker Compose mounts this into
# the backend container at /downloads so downloaded files appear on your desktop.
# Uncomment ONE line below and fill in your actual path — do not use ${HOME},
# it is unset on native Windows (cmd/PowerShell) and silently resolves to an
# empty string there, leaving DOWNLOADS_ROOT_HOST pointing at the wrong folder.
#
# Linux / macOS:
#   DOWNLOADS_ROOT_HOST=/home/yourname/Downloads
#
# Windows — Docker Desktop (WSL2 back-end) translates Windows paths
# (use forward slashes; Docker Desktop handles the conversion):
#   DOWNLOADS_ROOT_HOST=C:/Users/YourName/Downloads
#
# Required — `docker compose up` refuses to start without it. In the app's
# Settings → Download Location, set the SAME absolute path — the backend only
# ever writes through this bind mount (playlists get their own subfolder
# inside it, everything else goes directly into it), and rejects any other
# path while running in Docker.

# ── CORS allowlist (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of frontend origins allowed to call this API. Defaults
# to http://localhost:5173 and http://127.0.0.1:5173 (the Vite dev server's
# own origins) when unset. Only needed if you run the frontend on a different
# port or host.
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
